cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below, and record the exact commit you used.
title: 'NeumannCosine: Neumann cosine series on an interval and the discrete Neumann Laplacian in Lean 4'
type: software
authors:
- family-names: Chen
  given-names: Le
  affiliation: Auburn University
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/chenle02/neumann-cosine-lean
abstract: Lean 4 library on Neumann cosine series on [0, L] and the discrete Neumann Laplacian.
  It proves orthogonality of the modes, closed forms for integrals of products of modes and of
  absolutely summable cosine series, absolute summability and pointwise convergence of cosine
  expansions under W^{2,1} or H^2 Neumann hypotheses, basic one-dimensional weak-derivative
  results, the cosine eigenbasis of the reflected three-point Laplacian, and convergence of
  discrete eigenvalues and modal minima to their continuum values.
keywords:
- Lean 4
- Mathlib
- formalization
- Fourier cosine series
- Neumann boundary condition
- discrete Laplacian
